    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0359" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/4a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-18T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1928—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>26. The Department anticipates a repetition shortly by Buell<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d198-f1"/> of his charges concerning the Firestone concession and
                    the American loan in the lectures he plans delivering at the Williamstown
                    Institute of Politics. The advisability of preparing a statement in refutation,
                        <pb facs="0360" n="250" xml:id="pg250"/> along the lines of the telegram
                        Hines<anchor n="26" xml:id="d198-f2"/> recently sent Firestone, is, so the
                    Department understands, being discussed by Hines with President King. If the
                    latter should desire to issue a statement for distribution to the American press
                    on the subject, you should inform the President of Liberia that the Associated
                    Press is ready to handle his statement which should be sent by him as a direct
                    message to the Associated Press, with a request for appropriate publicity for
                    the statement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d198-f1" n="25" xml:id="d198-f1-content">
                <p>Raymond Leslie Buell, author of <hi rendition="#italic">The Native Problem in
                        Africa</hi> (New York, 1928).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d198-f2" n="26" xml:id="d198-f2-content">
                <p>W. D. Hines, Firestone representative in Liberia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
